From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:40:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 189/207] dsv41: map a field only where its kept bytes have
 established raw provenance

T5's r11 review blocked 2e0e7a0f2 / 2cc129bc1 on two HTTP counterexamples:
- the unique-substring search found the final U+FFFD (raw FF at byte 0) inside a
  tool argument the parse cut, at raw byte 42, and published dropped_lead 42;
- a raw anchor of 2^63 slipped past bound through `int64() orelse return`.

mapOf now maps the final field only onto a raw run whose outside is nothing but
blanks and whole tool envelopes (tool_parse.envelopes), the bytes the reply's
transforms delete. An envelope across the run's edge means the run is in cut
text. Two fitting runs, or raw bytes that are not valid UTF-8, give null.
bound nulls a field's map for any non-null raw coordinate that is not an i64
offset in [0, raw_bytes]; a null coordinate still leaves the map alone.

(cherry picked from commit 62802efef25f3f97dfe6f0e46288b05593feac3a)
